    summary_en: "As the cost of cyberattacks is projected to reach €5.5 trillion in 2021, hardware and software products face increasing cybersecurity risks. Current EU regulations largely fail to cover most digitally-enabled products, particularly non-embedded software, leading to widespread product vulnerabilities and inconsistent security update mechanisms. To address this issue, the EU has proposed the Cyber Resilience Act. This Act aims to mandate that manufacturers enhance product security from the product design and development stage throughout the entire product lifecycle. Its goals include establishing a unified cybersecurity framework, increasing transparency regarding product security attributes, and helping businesses and consumers use these products safely, thereby fundamentally improving the cybersecurity resilience of the entire internal market.",
